ENGROVE AUDIO LAB | ALIEN LT WAND | K2 GRADED 1
Independent engineering study based on Accepted Wand V3 R3.
Assembly STEP: Wand_K2_Graded_1_Study.step   Units: mm, g, gf, mL.
STEP SHA-256: c30f1f7f300cff19718ec62b6f85071cd351ca0c313e7bb395bbae2e94e77ad6
Pose record: h145-K2grade1-clear-setup.json   SHA-256: 9c878a7212ab05c8eeefccf05f7e6af4ec9f62d27c09c374380937a12aa17487

01  FRAME AND PRIMARY SHAPE
    Stylus tip neutral = (0,0,0). X aft, +Z up, Y transverse. Positive-Y
    skin is W02, negative-Y W01. Vertical pitch datum: (237.10,0,0).
    Neutral shaft/bore axis: X237.10, Z1.50, parallel to Y. The K2 outer
    mould is the original R3 Cobra shape, from X -8.00 to about +304.99.
    Use the exchange assembly for solid surface geometry and exact hardware
    positions. Machine the nominal reference skin at the front and both wire
    ports. Keep separate Ti, films, cage, nuts, hardware and removable cup.
    The exchange shell has the reference wall and real machined surfaces.
    The cured wall around the fixed outer mould follows the schedule below.

02  TEXTILES, EPOXY AND CLOSED-SECTION LAYUP
    B = one CF-BR-40 braided ply, opened/cut as required to hold the local
        paired +45/-45 degree fibre directions relative to the X centreline.
    U = full-coverage axial ply from adjacent 15 mm strips of CF-TP-RB-80-15-10.
        Centre each course on the local 0-degree axis and stagger joints.
    Matrix WEST SYSTEM 105 / 205. Nominal Vf 0.50. Confirm cured thickness
    and actual angle on a coupon and in the tool. Reported dimensions assume
    this fibre fraction. Measure the formed angle against a local template.
    Stack order below runs INNER to OUTER, symmetric in every full zone.
      Baseline A:      B / U / B                      0.8160 mm
      Light front:    U / B / U                      0.5399 mm
      Aft thick zone: B / B / U / U / B / B          1.6320 mm
    Transition from A to the two local stacks at these X stations.
      X27..42   ramp A toward light front over 15 mm, X42..137 full.
      X137..158 ramp light front back to A over 21 mm.
      X170..195 ramp A toward aft stack over 25 mm, X195..278 full
               on eligible skin. X278..295 return to A over 17 mm.
    Longitudinal ramps represent staggered patch edges around the perimeter
    at 0, 1/4, 1/2, 3/4 and full coverage. Arrange whole textile pieces.
    Preserve the outer shape,
    trim each half to Y=0, then bond the matched halves. Do not fill shafts,
    nut slots, clamping split or wire passages with resin. Preserve the
    exact inner cage and contact lands. On both sides of the rear sleeve,
    retain base stack A and multiply only the extra aft plies by the
    radial taper: 0 at r≤20, (r−20)/7 at 20<r<27, 1 at r≥27, with
    r=sqrt((X−286)^2+Y^2). Apply this to the longitudinal patch coverage.
    Recut the gauge diameters at Ø30.20 sleeve bore, Ø14.20 pitch
    saddle and Ø10.16 side-trim seats. This prescription excludes bonded
    darts or local fillets from the dry numerical geometry.

    Use staggered, close-fitting panel edges for the nominal mass. Purchased
    cutting scrap stays off the arm. Optional laps measured on the CAD mould
    add cured mass: 1 mm edge lap of 15 mm UD courses, +0.358 g. A 5 mm
    interrupted hoop lap adds +0.676 g per one braid layer across the four
    longitudinal transition bands or +0.165 g per one equivalent UD layer.
    In combination these details add about 1.199 g, with an independently
    calculated +2.578 g counterfill correction before any actual reweigh.

03  FRONT INTERFACE AND REAL LEAD PASSAGES
    Titanium mount plate 0.80, Z17.30..18.10, and a separate film to Z18.20.
    In both shell floors cut a capsule-shaped 8.80 × 2.80 longitudinal slot.
    The arc centres are X7.20 and 13.20 at Y±6.35, end radii 1.40. Retain
    the original slot shape of the Ti plate. Full screw travel: ±3.00 mm.
    Cage feet at Z19.10, Z19.05 skin lands, 0.050-mm adhesive only on the
    matching flat footprints (18.185 mm² per side). Cage and M2.5 sliding
    nut are captive. Keep the nut free of adhesive. Washer Ø4.20/2.80 × 0.15 between
    REV G flange and screw head. Top of washer Z14.45. Screw Ø2.50 × 7.00
    under head, head Ø3.60 × 1.00. STEP uses nominal thread envelopes.
    Full neutral nut engagement 2.00, tip-to-cage-roof clearance 0.30.
    At X40.0 and X226.8, Y=0, machine a round-ended through-slot into each
    local sole from below, width in X 1.50, length in Y 2.80. Edge-finish
    and insulate. Mask extra plies within 2 mm and stagger over 14 mm.
    The four Ø0.32 C03 leads have ≥0.4227 mm dry wire/skin clearance.

04  OPENABLE PITCH BEARING
    Machine one integral P01 in 7075-T6 with Ø14 middle barrel from Y -19..+19.
    At each end form Ø18 collars |Y|19..24. Line bore Ø12.04 continuously.
    Cut a 0.80-wide split to |Y|24, rounding its inner end at |Y|18.50.
    Clamp bolt axes parallel to X at Y±21.50, Z10.80. Smooth near hole Ø2.70,
    M2.5 opposite ear, bearing spotface Ø4.80 under each head. Use steel M2.5
    screws, 8.00 under head, Ø4.50 × 2.40 head, hex 2.00 A/F. Each screw
    has 3.40 mm effective tapped engagement. Install bare housing upwards
    through the saddle before bringing the assembly to the stationary carrier.
    Restrict the 0.10-mm radial adhesive bond to |Y|≤17. Fit clockable 7075
    P02, Ø12.00/11.00 × 49.00. Centre, rotate, then tighten both clamps.
    Nominal released radial gap 0.020. Maximum available bearing area at
    either end 185.121 mm². Pressure distribution and torque need measurement.
    K2 uses R3 magnetic poles and carrier. P05/P06/P07 are fixed references.
    Net P01 8.42961 g, P02 2.48725 g, each steel screw 0.57255 g.

05  BALANCED ASSEMBLY POSE
    Left/right trim axial travel shown relative to their R3 neutral station:
    +0.00000 mm. Cup lift: +1.42729 mm relative to R3.
    Cup centre X286. Nominal internal bore Ø23.00, four chambers with
    webs and floor. Physical filled height 27.393349 mm above the inner floor.
    Modelled mixture mass 51.848069 g, nominal volume 10.390929 mL,
    reopened four-chamber envelope 10.390929 mL. Use Ø1.00 steel shot
    and oil. For a dry packed density of 4.6 g/mL (solid steel
    7.8 g/mL, oil 0.95 g/mL), weigh 47.79827 g dry shot and add
    4.26295 mL oil to the pores. Four bulk solids represent the co-moving mixture.
    Rebalance by weighing
    the packed shot and oil, moving the trim/cup and checking a stylus gauge.
    Simulated tracking force 1.750000 gf and moving system mass 152.93661 g
    for this case. Cartridge assembly is the complete Goldring 1042 REV G.

06  RELATION TO FINITE-ELEMENT GEOMETRY
    Flexible reference skin contains the two pickup slots. Its effective material
    cards reference a uniform 0.8-mm integration thickness. The original front
    and saddle lands measure 0.850 mm at the centre. It does not explicitly mesh
    every local cured thickness, staggered drop, detailed thread or the two
    post-cure wire passages (6.2094 mm³ removed in the exported article).
    The final solved case includes the 20–27 mm sleeve keep-out in the
    material distribution. Actual lap mass, local resin and fabrication
    tolerances should be measured before the final tracking adjustment.
    The finite clamp uses a partial-contact tangent law. The STEP represents
    dry machining dimensions without preload deformation. Cueing and dust-cover
    clearance, laminate coupons, clamp retention and vibration acceptance
    require the built article. R3 remains the accepted design.
